From 487a71057701dffb8dd6ce9a283ddd30c6edb363 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: divinehawk <9158262+divinehawk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:04:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] session: Emit SelectedUserChanged when the user name changes

The Greeter interface declares a SelectedUserChanged signal, but it has
not been emitted since GdmSession was ported to GDBus in commit
53e24b49b, so the greeter never learns about a user name that a PAM
module sets during the conversation.

This happens with smartcard login without a user name: pam_sss with
allow_missing_name looks up the user from the certificate and sets
PAM_USER before asking for the PIN. Emitting the signal lets the greeter
show which user is being logged in, as it does when the user is picked
from the user list.

Part-of: <https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gdm/-/merge_requests/405>
---
 daemon/gdm-session.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/daemon/gdm-session.c b/daemon/gdm-session.c
index f36366e3c..180d1e1fe 100644
--- a/daemon/gdm-session.c
+++ b/daemon/gdm-session.c
@@ -1031,6 +1031,11 @@ worker_on_username_changed (GdmDBusWorker          *worker,
 
         gdm_session_select_user (self, (strlen (username) > 0) ? g_strdup (username) : NULL);
         gdm_session_defaults_changed (self);
+
+        if (self->greeter_interface != NULL) {
+                gdm_dbus_greeter_emit_selected_user_changed (self->greeter_interface,
+                                                             username);
+        }
 }
 
 static void
